---
import "../styles/global.css";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Contributing · OSS Maintainer Insights</title>
    <link rel="icon" href={`${base}favicon.svg`} type="image/svg+xml" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">
      Skip to content
    </a>
    <header class="topbar wrap">
      <a class="brand" href={base}>
        <span class="brand-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          ◈
        </span>
        <span>
          OSS Maintainer <strong>Insights</strong>
        </span>
      </a>
      <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
        <a href={base}>Explore repositories</a>
        <a href={`${base}collections/`}>Collections</a>
      </nav>
    </header>
    <main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="wrap methodology">
      <p class="eyebrow">CONTRIBUTE A PROJECT</p>
      <h1>
        A longer view
        <br />
        <em>starts with a proposal.</em>
      </h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Request complete 90-day creation windows and future historical tracking
        for a public GitHub repository.
      </p>
      <section class="panel">
        <h2>Open a catalog pull request</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Fork OSS Maintainer Insights and create a branch.</li>
          <li>
            Add the canonical <code>owner/repository</code> name to{" "}
            <code>catalog/repositories.json</code>. Choose OpenSSF, CNCF, or
            Community as the group.
          </li>
          <li>
            Run the documented local checks. Keep repository documentation and
            PR text in English.
          </li>
          <li>
            Open a PR explaining the project, its foundation association, and
            why tracking it would be useful.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          <a href="https://github.com/cpanato/oss-maintainer-insights/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">
            Read the full contribution guide ↗
          </a>
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="https://github.com/cpanato/oss-maintainer-insights/edit/main/catalog/repositories.json">
            Propose a catalog entry on GitHub ↗
          </a>
        </p>
      </section>
      <section class="panel">
        <h2>Catalog inclusion is not complete history</h2>
        <p>
          Scheduled Go collection enumerates every eligible PR created in a
          90-day window and resumes until complete. Historical ingestion and
          monthly trends are in development; a merged catalog entry does not
          immediately have complete history. The UI must show collection dates,
          coverage, and pending work.
        </p>
        <p>
          Only public repositories are eligible. Do not submit tokens, raw API
          payloads, or generated checkpoints. The collector never runs code from
          monitored repositories. Reviewers verify identity, API access, and
          collection cost; network failures remain inconclusive.
        </p>
      </section>
      <p>
        <a href={base}>← Back to repository exploration</a>
      </p>
    </main>
    <footer class="wrap">
      <p>Observed activity. Transparent coverage.</p>
      <p>No health scores · No maintainer roster inferred</p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
